# Unity Scripts

## MonoBehaviour budget
- Thin: hold `[SerializeField]` refs and forward to plain logic/services
- Do not put timers, pooling, or feature FSMs in `Update`/`LateUpdate` on views
- Prefab views expose refs once; consumers call `Show`/`Hide`/`Play`, not discover children at runtime

## GetComponent
- Avoid runtime `GetComponent` / `GetComponentInChildren` in hot paths and feature Tick
- Prefer SerializeField wired in prefab/editor builder
- One-time factory resolve on Instantiate is OK (`GetComponent` after spawn); do not re-query every frame
- World queries (`GetComponentInParent` on hit collider) OK only for collision/damage/surface resolution

## Prefabs & VFX
- Author VFX as Resources prefabs (particles, materials, refs) — no runtime particle bootstrap/utilities
- Services own pools, active lists, timing, and `Tick`; views are dumb
- Tick VFX services from both `GameplayBootstrap` and `HubBootstrap` when registered in gameplay context
- Config knobs live in ScriptableObjects under `Configs/`, not magic numbers scattered in views

## Example
```csharp
// ❌ BAD — MB owns timers + pool return
void Update() { _life -= dt; if (_life <= 0) _onDone(this); }

// ✅ GOOD — service Ticks; view only Show/Hide
_hitImpacts.Tick(deltaTime);
```
